{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 was received as 0xff (idle) per TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5 with tohost FAIL 0xdead. Per CONE_SLICE picosoc/picosoc.v:190 simpleuart instance and picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 module, TX bit timing in excerpt line 130 uses (cfg_divider >> 4) making TX 16x too fast versus divider 64, so TX returns to idle before RX samples and RX reads 0xff.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,10 +125,10 @@
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart loopback 0xa5 matches, no TRAP mismatch"}

